{
  "_notes": "Fixed park facilities (M3 depth). Each exists at tier 0 from day one at the world position given in parcels.json; higher tiers are bought IN ORDER from the General Store -> Upgrades tab. Every tier carries `effects`: a map of effect key -> ABSOLUTE value at that tier (not an increment). `effect_key` is the facility's headline effect for cards and tooltips; extra keys in `effects` (e.g. a diner's satisfaction bump) count too. Effect keys read by the economy: parking_capacity = visitors/day above front_gate_capacity; gate_capacity = extra gate throughput (Park Tram); concession_spend = multiplier on balance.revenue.per_visitor_concession_spend (food + gift add together, still needs concessions staff); satisfaction = added visitor satisfaction (raises price tolerance, capped by balance.attendance.satisfaction_price_tolerance_cap); appeal_bonus = added to the park appeal multiplier; education = Fact Book extras level (1 field notes, 2 your-specimens notes); illness_reduction = chance to avert an illness event, stacking with vets; heal_bonus = extra health/day for every dinosaur; management_capacity = staff the office can run before the over-capacity morale penalty in staff.json; event_mitigation = chance the office heads off any negative event. `render` is visual only: lot = { surface: dirt|gravel|asphalt|lined|overflow, w (tiles), rows (car rows), blocks (1 or 2 stall blocks), lamps }; building = { w, h (fraction of the max footprint), z (height in tiles), roofs (roof sections), storeys, style }. `short` is the code used on the Reports facility-tier tile. Phase 2b: appeal saturation compresses appeal_bonus and satisfaction effects to near-zero ROI on the reference parks (raw appeal 2.5+ above threshold 1.5), so non-concession facilities now carry a small secondary concession_spend (a snack counter in the restrooms, a souvenir rack at the visitor center, vending machines in the office, a gift kiosk at the tram stop). These are secondary effects (effect_key stays the same), so they do NOT count as concession stores and do NOT require extra concessions staff. Costs are tuned so each tier's 6-quarter wealth delta on its reference park exceeds the purchase price.",
